pthreads: reclaim unjoined threads while the main thread is blocked

A thread that ends without being joined on the main runtime thread (a
detached thread, or one another thread joins) was reclaimed only when the
main thread's event loop handled a CMD_CLEANUP_THREAD message. A main
thread that stays blocked in emscripten_futex_wait() never did, so each
such thread kept its stack, TLS and struct, and its Worker never went back
to the pool. Hand those threads to the main thread through a lock-free
list instead, which it drains whenever it processes its queued calls,
including inside emscripten_futex_wait(); the message is still sent, for
a main thread that is idle in its event loop.

Since a wait on the main thread can now free a thread, dlopen()'s sync,
which waits on each thread of a list it took first, holds the cleanups
off until it has been through the list, then runs them. A thread that
has ended meanwhile stays allocated and refuses the proxy, as it did
before; one already gone at its turn is skipped as well.

